{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "eaf72464-f7dd-43a7-ba96-eef1c70b8506",
    "name": "Quipu Transformation Service",
    "description": "Complete REST API collection for the Quipu Transformation Service microservice (port 3036). This is the ETL engine of the platform: extracts raw data from heterogeneous sources, transforms it into a knowledge graph (nodes + relationships), and loads it into Neo4j, Yugabyte, and Synapse Kafka; also materializes data to Hive/Trino for analytical querying.\n\nPipeline shape: source -> shape parse -> metadata extract -> schema graph -> CTAS (Trino) -> Parquet on S3 -> parquet read + validate -> Yugabyte COPY (journal/node/edge state) -> Synapse Kafka -> Neo4j.\n\nCollection variables:\n- {{baseUrl}}  — default http://localhost:3036\n- {{token}}    — bearer/JWT-like token sent as Authorization header\n- {{tenantId}} — tenant identifier (X-Tenant-ID header)\n\nNotes:\n- Endpoints in '02 — Connection' and '05 — File Upload (S3)' require the exact versioned media type as Content-Type (application/vnd.quipu.connection+json;version=1.0.0 and application/vnd.quipu.file-upload+json;version=1.0.0 respectively) — Spring returns 415 otherwise.\n- 'DataSourceModel.driverType' must be one of: SNOWFLAKE, DB2, POSTGRES, BIGQUERY, MYSQL, SQLITE, MONGO, CASSANDRA, NEO4J, CSV, ORACLE, EXCEL, PDF, MARIADB, JSON.\n- Several endpoints (Hive/Trino creation & removal, sample-record upload) are fire-and-forget: they return 200 immediately while work continues on a background executor.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56383100",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56383100-eaf72464-f7dd-43a7-ba96-eef1c70b8506?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — Atomic Ingestion",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ingest Streams",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Tenant-ID",
                "value": "{{tenantId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Refresh-Token",
                "value": "",
                "disabled": true
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "[\n  {\n    \"id\": 1,\n    \"name\": \"customer_stream\",\n    \"description\": \"Customer ingest\",\n    \"streamLabels\": [\"Customer\"],\n    \"sqlQuery\": \"SELECT * FROM customers\",\n    \"cypherQuery\": \"MERGE (c:Customer {id: row.id})\",\n    \"streamType\": \"DBT-NODE\",\n    \"realmId\": 1001,\n    \"deleted\": false,\n    \"tablesInfo\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": 1,\n        \"tableName\": \"customers\",\n        \"tableUri\": \"s3://bucket/customers.parquet\",\n        \"query\": \"SELECT * FROM customers\",\n        \"dataSourceId\": 5\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event/ingest?truncate=false&seedSequenceFromJournal=false&forceIngest=false",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "event",
                "ingest"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "truncate",
                  "value": "false"
                },
                {
                  "key": "seedSequenceFromJournal",
                  "value": "false"
                },
                {
                  "key": "forceIngest",
                  "value": "false"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Event-sourced ingestion of atomic (DBT-NODE) streams into the journal/state pipeline. Base path /event."
    },
